From: T4 Linux port
Subject: [PATCH] bt532_ts: emit classic ABS_X/ABS_Y + BTN_TOUCH for X11/evdev

The Zinitix bt532 touchscreen driver only reports multitouch
(ABS_MT_*) axes. Xorg's xf86-input-evdev wants a classic absolute
touchscreen (ABS_X/ABS_Y + BTN_TOUCH) to drive the core pointer and
emulate clicks for a window manager like XFCE.

This patch mirrors the first finger (slot 0) onto the classic axes and
toggles BTN_TOUCH on press/release, and registers the classic axes at
probe time (both orientation branches). Multitouch reporting is left
intact, so libinput still sees the full MT stream.

Applies to: Sabsabsab/android_kernel_samsung_degas3g (3.10)
File: drivers/input/touchscreen/bt532_ts.c

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/bt532_ts.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/bt532_ts.c
@@ <report loop, finger present, after MT report> @@
 		input_report_abs(info->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_X, x);
 		input_report_abs(info->input_dev, ABS_MT_POSITION_Y, y);
+		/* T4-X11: drive X pointer from first finger */
+		if (i == 0) {
+			input_report_abs(info->input_dev, ABS_X, x);
+			input_report_abs(info->input_dev, ABS_Y, y);
+			input_report_key(info->input_dev, BTN_TOUCH, 1);
+		}
 	} else if (zinitix_bit_test(sub_status, SUB_BIT_UP) ||
 		zinitix_bit_test(prev_sub_status, SUB_BIT_EXIST)) {
 		...
 		input_mt_slot(info->input_dev, i);
 		input_mt_report_slot_state(info->input_dev, MT_TOOL_FINGER, 0);
+		/* T4-X11 */
+		if (i == 0)
+			input_report_key(info->input_dev, BTN_TOUCH, 0);
 	} else {
 		...

@@ <probe, axis registration> @@
 	if (pdata->orientation & TOUCH_XY_SWAP) {
 		... ABS_MT_POSITION_X/Y ...
+		/* T4-X11: classic axes for Xorg evdev (swapped) */
+		input_set_abs_params(info->input_dev, ABS_Y,
+			info->cap_info.MinX,
+			info->cap_info.MaxX + ABS_PT_OFFSET, 0, 0);
+		input_set_abs_params(info->input_dev, ABS_X,
+			info->cap_info.MinY,
+			info->cap_info.MaxY + ABS_PT_OFFSET, 0, 0);
 	} else {
 		... ABS_MT_POSITION_X/Y ...
+		/* T4-X11: classic axes for Xorg evdev */
+		input_set_abs_params(info->input_dev, ABS_X,
+			info->cap_info.MinX,
+			info->cap_info.MaxX + ABS_PT_OFFSET, 0, 0);
+		input_set_abs_params(info->input_dev, ABS_Y,
+			info->cap_info.MinY,
+			info->cap_info.MaxY + ABS_PT_OFFSET, 0, 0);
 	}
+	set_bit(BTN_TOUCH, info->input_dev->keybit);

Notes / gotchas learned on-device:
 * With ABS_X/Y present AND BTN_TOUCH set, evdev reports
   "Found absolute touchscreen" + "Configuring as touchscreen" and the
   pointer follows the finger with click emulation.
 * We actually ended up driving X via libinput (udev-tagged
   ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN=1), which reads the MT stream directly; the
   classic-axes patch is still useful if you fall back to evdev.
 * The same input device also carries the capacitive Back (KEY_BACK,
   158) and Recents (BTN_4, 254) keys; they surface as a second
   (keyboard) X input device.
